+## Audio Pipeline Invariants (tempo lane R1, DEF-001 / DEF-002)
+
+These bind every change to the audio producer, the tempo tracker and anything that gates a
+published audio decision. They exist because one fault (a hidden silence veto on twice-compressed
+novelty) was diagnosed, patched symptomatically, tombstoned and lost in August 2026, then found
+again 70 days later (`docs/defects/DEF-001-tempo-hidden-silence-veto.md`). Each invariant names
+the gate that enforces it; `pytest -m tempo_gates` runs them all.
+
+- **I1 Published decisions carry their vetoes. No silent gate.** Every gate that can clear a
+  published decision (`locked`, `beat_tick`, confidence) sets a named veto bit (`K1TempoVeto`),
+  observable in `K1TempoDebugSnapshot` and the emulator stream. Gate: M1 veto observability.
+- **I2 One compression per signal.** `novelty_curve` is sqrt-domain for visuals; tempo reads its
+  own linear-domain field. No consumer re-compresses a shared signal. Gate: M2 contrast invariance.
+- **I3 Every fixed threshold names its calibration** (mic, distribution, fixture hash, date) in
+  the spec header (`audio/k1_tempo_spec.h`). A threshold without provenance is a defect, not a
+  constant.
+- **I4 A metric gates a published decision only with a committed held-out AUC receipt**
+  (`docs/receipts/tempo-lock-r1/conf_auc.json`, AUC >= 0.8 on dev and held-out). Gate: M3.
+- **I5 Corpus files carry a role** (`tests/fixtures/tempo_corpus/manifest.json`, `dev` |
+  `heldout`). The scorer refuses an acceptance verdict on dev-role files (exit 3); a tuned constant
+  records the manifest hash it was tuned on. Gate: M4.
+- **I6 Selection or confidence changes run the metrical trap suite.** A new attractor ratio
+  (2/3, 3/4, 4/3, 3/2, 3) is a regression even when Acc2 rises. Gate: M5.
+- **I7 Fixture bytes are captured from the production chain and shared**, never re-derived on
+  both sides (emulator `N` lines -> `scripts/regression-harness/tempo_lane_replay.py`).
+- **I8 A defect gets a ledger entry with a reproduction BEFORE any fix** (`docs/defects/`).
+  A tombstone closes a fix, never a defect; it must cite the DEF it leaves open.
+- **I9 The silence decision belongs to the producer** (`audio.silence`). The tracker may decay
+  history on silence; it may not invent a second silence from contrast.
+- **I10 Off-flag builds are byte-identical.** Every lane is a compile flag; constants live once,
+  in the spec header, and are edited by symbol (never by digit; each substituted token must
+  appear exactly once).
+
+**Known non-fixes (never repeat; commit 7d932083, tombstoned in 1bdf54d0):** scaling novelty by a
+constant to raise contrast; lowering `K1_LOCK_CONFIDENCE` or `K1_CONF_V2_REL` to obtain a lock;
+disabling the silence gate without replacing the silence source; gating any of these behind a
+mic identity.
+
